From f6b9cbc81c07a46d05bd00a1249984e93896f44f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:45:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the setting of HDR over the tunnel, and what
 the rule is fed with

videoscreen.hadeshdr10tunnel (level 2, on by default, shown where the connector has
DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TUNNEL_LAB): HDR10, HLG and HDR10+ as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits packed in the RGB 8 bpc
tunnel where the ordinary output would send 4:2:0 or RGB at 8 bits. On by default because the
bridge's part of it carries the picture exactly (host test, previous commit); off is the output as
it was.

HDR10Tunnel.h gets what the window will feed it with, as pure functions a test builds: LinkOf()
(DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT to the five links the rule knows; 4:4:4, an unknown depth and anything else
are "not known", which is a "no"), PictureTaken() (PQ or HLG, BT.2020 with its matrix for
non-constant luminance, progressive, 2D: what the bridge draws as it is) and IsHdrPicture() (not
Dolby Vision, which goes its own ways). Two reasons more in Decide(): a tunnel that failed on this
display (not tried again until it changes) and a colour format that the user chose (theirs, as the
rule of the driver for 4:2:0 steps aside for it). The order of the rest is the one of the first
version of the rule, and its host test (51271 checks) still passes.

Host test of the rule in both directions: every combination of its eleven booleans, eight rates,
four sizes and five links against the rule written the other way round (327680 combinations), each
reason alone, and undone; EDID without 4:2:2, 1080p, 2160p24 and 2160p30, 4096x2160, a refusal,
the user's format, HDR10+, HLG, Dolby Vision as HDR10, native Dolby Vision; eleven mutants of the
header are caught. Strings 41400 and 41401 (core), 33000 and 33001 (Estuary), English and
Spanish. Not tried on hardware.
